  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Suppose $a$ is coprime to 10. Since $\\phi(10)=4$, Euler’s Theorem says that $a^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}$. That is, the units digit of $a^4$ is always 1. Using this fact, find the units digit of:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 4,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$333^4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "1",
          "worked": "Since 333 is coprime to 10, Euler’s theorem gives $$333^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}.$$ The units digit is 1.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$123^5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "3",
          "worked": "Since 123 is coprime to 10, $123^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}$. $$\\begin{align*}123^5&=123^4\\times123\\\\123^5&\\equiv1\\times3\\pmod{10}\\\\123^5&\\equiv3\\pmod{10}\\end{align*}$$ The units digit is 3.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$23^{32}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "1",
          "worked": "Since 23 is coprime to 10, $23^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}$. $$\\begin{align*}23^{32}&=(23^4)^8\\\\23^{32}&\\equiv1^8\\pmod{10}\\\\23^{32}&\\equiv1\\pmod{10}\\end{align*}$$ The units digit is 1.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$123^{321}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "3",
          "worked": "Since 123 is coprime to 10, $123^4\\equiv1\\pmod{10}$. $$\\begin{align*}123^{321}&=(123^4)^{80}\\times123\\\\123^{321}&\\equiv1^{80}\\times3\\pmod{10}\\\\123^{321}&\\equiv3\\pmod{10}\\end{align*}$$ The units digit is 3.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
